---
/* Privacy policy, English (FR-45). It describes what the site does today. When the contact form
   starts sending (PSP 5.2), add the sections for the form, Cloudflare Turnstile and Resend here and
   in de/datenschutz.astro (FT-45 checks for the form and Turnstile sections). */
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { OPERATOR, UPDATED } from '../i18n/legal.js';
---

<LegalPage lang="en" title="Privacy policy - re.verb one" heading="Privacy policy" enHref="/privacy" deHref="/de/datenschutz">
  <p class="legal-sub">Last updated: {UPDATED.en}</p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The controller under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is {OPERATOR.name}, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. In short</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets no cookies, uses no analytics or tracking tools and shows no advertising. Personal
    data is processed only as far as it is needed to deliver the site and to answer you when you
    write to us.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted by Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Avenue #4133, Covina, CA 91723, USA. When you
    open a page, your browser sends technical data that the server records in log files:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your IP address</li>
    <li>date and time of the request</li>
    <li>the page or file requested</li>
    <li>the referring page, if your browser sends it</li>
    <li>browser type and operating system (user agent)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This is needed to deliver the site and to keep it secure, for example to detect and prevent
    attacks. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in a secure and working
    website). Vercel processes this data on our behalf under a data processing agreement (Art. 28
    GDPR) and keeps the logs for a limited period. Data may be transferred to the USA. Vercel is
    certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, for which an adequacy decision of the European
    Commission exists (Art. 45 GDPR); in addition, its agreement includes the EU Standard Contractual
    Clauses. More: <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">Vercel privacy notice</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    The fonts (Archivo and Unbounded) are served from this site's own domain. Your browser makes no
    connection to Google or any other font provider.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Settings stored in your browser</h2>
  <p>
    When you choose a language or a colour theme, the site saves that choice in your browser's local
    storage (keys <code>lang</code> and <code>theme</code>), so the site opens the same way next time.
    The values stay on your device and are not sent to us. You can delete them at any time in your
    browser settings. The legal basis is § 25(2) no. 2 of the German Telecommunications Digital
    Services Data Protection Act (TDDDG): the storage is strictly necessary for the function you asked for.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Contact by email</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we process your email address, your name if you give it, and your message to
    answer you. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR if your request concerns a contract or its
    preparation, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering enquiries). We delete
    the data when it is no longer needed, unless a legal retention period applies.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Link to GitHub</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to the owner's profile on GitHub. GitHub receives data about you only when you
    follow that link. Its own privacy statement then applies.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right of access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17),
    restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20) and to object to processing based
    on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Art. 21). To use these rights, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{OPERATOR.email}</a>. You can also lodge a complaint with a data
    protection supervisory authority, in particular in the EU member state where you live or work
    (Art. 77 GDPR).
  </p>
</LegalPage>
